This repository contains changes to the INET EligibilityTimeMeter source file to implement a π² (Processing-in-Interconnect) synapse mapped 
onto the IEEE 802.1Qcr Asynchronous Traffic Shaper (ATS) protocol, simulated in OMNeT++/INET over a TsnLinearNetwork. 
The omnetpp.ini file tests the π² synapse mapped to ATS with two traffic classes (Best Effort and Video) metered at the switch ingress 
via EligibilityTimeMeter and shaped at egress via Ieee8021qAsynchronousShaper.

Running the Simulation
1. Copy EligibilityTimeMeter.cc into <INET_ROOT>/src/inet/protocolelement/shaper/ and rebuild INET.
2. Place omnetpp.ini in your project directory.
3. Run the simulation

The change to EligibilityTimeMeter.cc is as follows:
Change 1 — meterPacket(): The standard ATS eligibility time computation:
eligibilityTime = max(arrivalTime, groupEligibilityTime, schedulerEligibilityTime)
is replaced with:
eligibilityTime = arrivalTime + maxResidenceTime   // T1
